401 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (THIS CODE IS A LEXICAL ANALYZER \(LEXER\), DESIGNED TO PROCESS A PASCAL-LIKE PROGRAMMING LANGUAGE. IT ANALYZES SOURCE CODE AND BREAKS IT INTO TOKENS SUCH AS KEYWORDS \(PROGRAM, IF, VAR\), IDENTIFIERS, NUMBERS, STRINGS, AND OPERATORS WHILE IGNORING WHITESPACE AND COMMENTS. IT MAINTAINS A SYMBOL TABLE TO TRACK DECLARED VARIABLES AND PREVENT DUPLICATES. THE LEXER WORKS WITH A SUBSEQUENT PARSER TO VALIDATE SYNTAX, RETURNING EACH TOKEN WITH ITS ASSOCIATED VALUE \(E.G., VARIABLE NAMES OR NUMBERS\) VIA YYLVAL.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
