492 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (THIS YACC \(BISON\) PARSER, WRITTEN IN C, ANALYZES A PASCAL-LIKE PROGRAMMING LANGUAGE, BEGINNING WITH DECLARATIONS FOR STANDARD LIBRARIES, FUNCTION PROTOTYPES LIKE YYERROR \(ERROR REPORTING\), YYLEX \(LEXICAL ANALYSIS\), INSERT_SYMBOL \(SYMBOL TABLE MANAGEMENT\), AND PRINT_PRODUCTION \(DEBUGGING OUTPUTS\). THE %TOKEN DIRECTIVES DEFINE LEXICAL TOKENS \(PROGRAM, ID, IF, ETC.\), WHILE %UNION SPECIFIES TOKEN VALUE TYPES. GRAMMAR RULES ENFORCE THE LANGUAGE STRUCTURE, INCLUDING PROGRAM ENTRY \(PROGRAM\), TYPE/VARIABLE DECLARATIONS, EXPRESSIONS, PROCEDURES/FUNCTIONS, AND CONTROL STATEMENTS \(IF, WHILE, FOR\), WITH SEMANTIC ACTIONS ENABLING SYMBOL TABLE UPDATES OR LOGGING. THE YYERROR FUNCTION HANDLES SYNTAX ERRORS, AND MAIN INITIATES PARSING VIA YYPARSE\(\), COLLECTIVELY BUILDING A PARSER THAT VALIDATES AND PROCESSES PASCAL-LIKE SOURCE CODE.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
